I now have a complete picture of the codebase. Here is the full, detailed implementation plan.

---

## Implementation Plan: Identity Reset Detection UI

### Overview

The feature detects when a room member's identity has changed (pinned or verified state violated), shows a dismissible banner in the room timeline, and adds contextual actions in `MemberDetailsBottomSheet` and `RoomMembers`. The subscription is scoped to a single room via `room.subscribeToIdentityStatusChanges`, so it lives in a hook called from `RoomTimeline`, not in a global provider.

---

## 1. New Files to Create

### 1a. `src/modules/matrix-client/hooks/useRoomIdentityStatus.ts`

This hook is the core engine. It subscribes to the SDK listener for a specific room and exposes the current violation state and resolution actions.

```typescript
import { IdentityState } from "@unomed/react-native-matrix-sdk";
import { MatrixService } from "modules/matrix-client/services";
import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";

export type IdentityViolation = {
  userId: string;
  displayName: string;
  state: IdentityState.PinViolation | IdentityState.VerificationViolation;
};

export const useRoomIdentityStatus = (roomId: string) => {
  const [violations, setViolations] = useState<IdentityViolation[]>([]);
  const taskHandleRef = useRef<{ cancel?: () => void } | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const room = MatrixService.instance?.getRoom(roomId);
    if (!room) return;

    let cancelled = false;

    const setup = async () => {
      const handle = await room.subscribeToIdentityStatusChanges({
        call: (changes) => {
          if (cancelled) return;
          setViolations((prev) => {
            const updated = [...prev];
            for (const change of changes) {
              const idx = updated.findIndex((v) => v.userId === change.userId);
              if (
                change.changedTo === IdentityState.PinViolation ||
                change.changedTo === IdentityState.VerificationViolation
              ) {
                // Fetch display name from room members or fall back to userId
                const displayName = change.userId; // resolved below via member lookup
                const entry: IdentityViolation = {
                  userId: change.userId,
                  displayName,
                  state: change.changedTo,
                };
                if (idx !== -1) updated[idx] = entry;
                else updated.push(entry);
              } else {
                // Verified or Pinned → clear violation
                if (idx !== -1) updated.splice(idx, 1);
              }
            }
            return [...updated];
          });
        },
      });
      taskHandleRef.current = handle;
    };

    setup().catch(console.error);

    return () => {
      cancelled = true;
      taskHandleRef.current?.cancel?.();
    };
  }, [roomId]);

  const pinUser = useCallback(
    async (userId: string) => {
      await MatrixService.pinUserIdentity(userId);
      setViolations((prev) => prev.filter((v) => v.userId !== userId));
    },
    [],
  );

  const withdrawAndResend = useCallback(
    async (userId: string) => {
      await MatrixService.withdrawVerificationAndResend(roomId, [userId]);
      setViolations((prev) => prev.filter((v) => v.userId !== userId));
    },
    [roomId],
  );

  const dismissViolation = useCallback((userId: string) => {
    setViolations((prev) => prev.filter((v) => v.userId !== userId));
  }, []);

  return { violations, pinUser, withdrawAndResend, dismissViolation };
};
```

**Design note on display names:** The SDK's `IdentityStatusChange` only provides `userId`. The hook should resolve display names from the room member list. In `setup`, after the subscription, call `room.members()` once to build a `Map<userId, displayName>` that `call()` can reference via a closure ref.

